<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Daniel O'Connell</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1775">1775</a>–<a href="/years/1847">1847</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Daniel O'Connell was an Irish political leader known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">the Liberator</a>. His Catholic Association organised mass, peaceful pressure that forced the British government to grant Catholic emancipation in 1829, and he then led a campaign for repeal of the Act of Union, which faltered after the government banned his monster meeting at Clontarf in 1843.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/daniel-oconnell.jpg" alt="Daniel O'Connell" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Mulrenin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Daniel_O%27Connell.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After <b>Daniel O’Connell</b>’s mass campaign, the Roman Catholic Relief Act of 1829 allowed Catholics to sit in Parliament.</blockquote><a href="/empire/united-kingdom-of-great-britain-and-ireland">United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>It was forced through by Wellington and Peel after <b>Daniel O'Connell</b>'s election in County Clare.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/april-13">13 April in history</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Cahersiveen, in what is now <a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a>. Died in Genoa, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=51.95,-10.22&amp;year=1821" aria-label="Cahersiveen on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4320 368 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Daniel O'Connell"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4770 638h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4770 638h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=51.95,-10.22&amp;year=1821">What was here in 1821? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
